  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "A group of students is asked if they enjoy Mathematics or English. It was established that if a member of the group is randomly chosen, then the probability that they enjoy Mathematics is 0.8, while the probability they enjoy English is 0.6. Also, the probability they enjoy both subjects is 0.5. Use this information to determine the probability that a randomly selected person from this group:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "does not enjoy English",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.4$",
          "worked": "Let $E$ be the event that the student enjoys English.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(E')&=1-\\Pr(E)\\\\\\Pr(E')&=1-0.6\\\\\\Pr(E')&=0.4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "does not enjoy Mathematics",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.2$",
          "worked": "Let $M$ be the event that the student enjoys Mathematics.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(M')&=1-\\Pr(M)\\\\\\Pr(M')&=1-0.8\\\\\\Pr(M')&=0.2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "does not enjoy Mathematics and does not enjoy English",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.1$\n\nUse the complement of enjoying at least one subject.",
          "worked": "Let $M$ and $E$ be the events that the student enjoys Mathematics and English respectively. Enjoying neither subject is the complement of $M\\cup E$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(M\\cup E)&=\\Pr(M)+\\Pr(E)-\\Pr(M\\cap E)\\\\\\Pr(M\\cup E)&=0.8+0.6-0.5\\\\\\Pr(M\\cup E)&=0.9\\\\\\Pr(M'\\cap E')&=1-\\Pr(M\\cup E)\\\\\\Pr(M'\\cap E')&=1-0.9\\\\\\Pr(M'\\cap E')&=0.1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "does not enjoy Mathematics or does not enjoy English.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.5$\n\nUse the complement of enjoying both subjects.",
          "worked": "Let $M$ and $E$ be the events that the student enjoys Mathematics and English respectively. The inclusive event $M'\\cup E'$ is the complement of enjoying both subjects.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(M'\\cup E')&=1-\\Pr(M\\cap E)\\\\\\Pr(M'\\cup E')&=1-0.5\\\\\\Pr(M'\\cup E')&=0.5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
